## Migrating a legacy App resource

Terraform 1.8 or later supports moving an `interfere_surface` resource into this resource. Keep the existing workspace slug and set `id` to the App's canonical service UUID. Replace the old resource configuration, then add:

```terraform
moved {
  from = interfere_surface.website
  to   = interfere_service.website
}
```

Run a normal `terraform plan` with refresh enabled. The provider preserves the old App identity during the offline state move and resolves its canonical service during refresh. Missing aliases, changed identities, and permission failures stop migration while preserving state. Migration creates no App, credential, or service, and never deletes retained telemetry. After a successful apply, remove the `moved` block when every workspace using the configuration has migrated.
